{"title":"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c99bbe74cccdc92b249d376f13d9429d41a8b7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />. The angle bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39a4406ab9a6a9f1d35009c2e18008d1888fc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAB$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3ad57710b6810476e6017ea2c2cc6d41219c218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> meet the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> be the incenter of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840cb55c82434b9ae047760636a017e9441e6ca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/a/f9ad63616bd49b87f4b738bc90b17d6a77352d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BEK=45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"107\" height=\"13\" />. Find all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39a4406ab9a6a9f1d35009c2e18008d1888fc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAB$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p><i>Authors: Jan Vonk and Peter Vandendriessche, Belgium, and Hojoo Lee, South Korea</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/154dc356150dad8272f4c66a7063852906863c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CK$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> to meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Then, we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the incenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/c/0bc2586476fd53eca164ea7beab806f43b528783.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IM=ID$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the intersection of the incircle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8d37413bae1973358eebff164711f292d16be56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/0728bebb477a2636300c56851b6a6f9e382c1b83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/6897f9109f92de29ec96d8aec5f25b61f2a2814f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle IDC \\cong \\triangle IMC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/0/7705eeb7b6859113c71b1c78ceb7057f434b6d25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle IMK = \\angle IDK = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"189\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>From here, there are two possibilities: either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> coincide or they don't. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> coincide, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/8068607716f3c2549af1dc978d77a422ca7201dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> is the median and the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/7/8d7518521be462abc8182d43c4419567358773ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is equilateral, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/757956f190570a9e1ac1665bff7eec4fa3d91759.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC = 60^\\circ$\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Otherwise, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/1/f213df85ca30fab691942ad03882b8070466c4f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MIKE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/5/c05f34210d5077ab5f47222a96ec98f124aa969e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle IME = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/f/51f69010cc07adcd7f79449395facf8bfc06b6e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IE$\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" /> is the diameter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/7/ed7f6bdd201eae4e54be3816e23c5bf1b63b6e7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(MIKE)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac9ae35add25159214a2351a9efdea8e50d4137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle IKE = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/a/33a673db40c61ef03d0d39a9a3d34f43a7ae1dfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle KIE = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/6/ce6ea2d242e1f8dd7e04de278fee03ab391f15b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BIC = 180^\\circ - \\angle KIE = 135^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"247\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2f3766e568267213651bd1e8b4494e11760035f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/343b725ebc8a5afabf09ec73bc1296ca9556396e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAB = 180^\\circ = 4x = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"210\" height=\"15\" />, which is the second possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39a4406ab9a6a9f1d35009c2e18008d1888fc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAB$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2009_IMO_P4_(1).png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/2/27/2009_IMO_P4_%281%29.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"768\" height=\"422\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will be using the trig bash solution given in EGMO.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the incenter, and set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d4961c73a8ff985dd2ea19b29fb4738d19298db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAC = 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/9167e7a81a116e2428c8230cb0f3e05efc821d23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x &lt; 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" />. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/c/90c7cf865a840a1cdc8387f3a2dda903b25e670e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AIE = \\angle DIC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"129\" height=\"14\" />, it is easy to compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/a/baafaaf57c92bed221b8322ed57b7356c78fe72b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle KIE = 90^\\circ - 2x, \\quad \\angle ECI = 45^\\circ - x, \\quad \\angle IEK = 45^\\circ, \\quad \\angle KEC = 3x.\\]\" width=\"545\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Then, by LoS, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a21b665b9edda9f1cc2e5061499315fd09c8e062.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{IK}{KC} = \\dfrac{\\sin 45^\\circ \\cdot \\frac{EK}{\\sin(90^\\circ - 2x)}}{\\sin(3x) \\cdot \\frac{EK}{\\sin(45^\\circ-x)}} = \\frac{\\sin 45^\\circ \\sin(45^\\circ - x)}{\\sin(3x) \\sin(90^\\circ-2x)}.\\]\" width=\"395\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Also, by the angle bisector theorem on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/d/d7dcc821446f7ae53565b35a10d83ec196d314ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle IDC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/548322b13aafc5770cf573a7df344d40fe7f25c8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{IK}{KC} = \\dfrac{ID}{DC} = \\frac{\\sin(45^\\circ-x)}{\\sin(45^\\circ+x)}.\\]\" width=\"217\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Equating the above two equations and cancelling <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/7106942c5385fb6a9f759e38f5900eee66f2a7f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(45^\\circ-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/423c29990bd01d3bf53278825478b49c90632136.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin 45^\\circ \\sin(45^\\circ+x)=\\sin 3x \\sin(90^\\circ - 2x).\\]\" width=\"328\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Applying product to sum, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe27ba196f6800b14749f193de78b32903a8329b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(x)-\\cos(90^\\circ+x) = \\cos(5x-90^\\circ)-\\cos(90^\\circ+x),\\]\" width=\"421\" height=\"18\" />\nor simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/916bc0c663687a11c0d60f78f6a7360cca09bea1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x = \\cos(5x-90^\\circ)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"20\" />. Then, applying difference to product, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/7/2d7e8f10ca4153407a3ff51923787dde14da8ecc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 = \\cos(5x-90^\\circ)-\\cos x = 2 \\sin(3x-45^\\circ) \\sin(2x-45^\\circ).\\]\" width=\"449\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Then, we get two cases: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/4/254ab9d4f5ebf8b8e41bdbdcd2023b236ea92d60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(3x-45^\\circ) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/789b95e430d2a4dd8eef24c67b495b2772fc6479.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(2x-45^\\circ) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />. Note that these hold iff the expressions inside the sines are multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c4460b5100c3ce982ab5ebb20a8c3871e9cfdc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />. Using the bound <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/9167e7a81a116e2428c8230cb0f3e05efc821d23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x &lt; 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" />, we can easily get that the only possible values are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/a/27a951ee8a776aef13a3a7fbc967ace3a9517a2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 15^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/f/aaf51b64af920f63c2297f8d6c6b57b68f57876c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{45}{2}^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"40\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef41fee8c19a7eb4295d9db36620b20e114932b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A = 60^\\circ, 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2009_IMO_P4_(2).png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/8/82/2009_IMO_P4_%282%29.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"390\" height=\"405\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO\" title=\"2009 IMO\">2009 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017221852\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.094 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 355/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11579/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.066      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.066      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8303:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017221852 and revision id 254996. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}